      "title": "Accepts tampered payload",
      "what": "D12 changed amount_paid from 2400 to 0 and was signed for the original body. Your handler returned 200 in 167 ms: orders.count 0 → 1, expected a 4xx and no change.",
      "why": "Stripe signs the exact bytes it sends. If a failed check doesn't stop the request, anyone who can reach this URL can make your handler act on content Stripe never sent.",
      "citation": {
        "label": "Stripe docs › Webhooks › Verify signatures",
        "url": "https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks#verify-official-libraries"
      },
      "fix": {
        "text": "Return 400 as soon as signature verification fails, before any write. After the fix, D12 should get 400 and leave orders.count at 0.",
        "snippet": "app.post('/webhooks/stripe', express.raw({ type: 'application/json' }), (req, res) => {\n  let event;\n  try {\n    event = stripe.webhooks.constructEvent(req.body, req.get('stripe-signature'), endpointSecret);\n  } catch (err) {\n    return res.status(400).send('Invalid signature'); // stop here, don't log and continue\n  }\n  // ...handle event\n});"
      },
      "likely_cause_text": "Late (D9) was rejected, so the timestamp check runs; the signature check probably fails into a log line instead of stopping the request."
    },
